    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who represents our strongest play with an elite score of 74.56. He holds a massive platoon advantage against Grant Holmes (4.71 xERA), with his elevated score driven by a combination of the hitter-friendly park factors and a prime #2 spot in the order. **Jacob Wilson** also provides significant upside (61.42) against Sonny Gray; despite facing a difficult arm, **Jacob Wilson**\u2019s leadoff status and park factors keep him well within the \"Strong\" start tier. Meanwhile, **Nasim Nunez** benefits from a strong matchup against the weak rotation of Holmes, making him a sneaky play despite his bottom-of-the-order assignment.\n\nRisk management is a significant theme today, particularly regarding the weather in the games involving **Liam Hicks**, **Jorge Polanco**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**, all of whom face a 35% rain risk. **Luis Robert Jr.**, in particular, saw his score dampened significantly to 49.15 due to a poor platoon matchup against Eury P\u00e9rez, though his ability to exploit P\u00e9rez\u2019s slow delivery keeps his stolen base potential relevant for our scarcity-driven strategy. The closest call for the final lineup spot was **Jackson Merrill** (55.61); while he narrowly missed the elite threshold, his stability in the #5 spot secured him a place over potential alternatives. We continue to monitor the status of **Jordan Westburg**, who remains sidelined on the IL, while league-leaders like **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson** are unavailable today due to schedule off-days, forcing us to rely on our depth to maintain efficiency in our 5x5 categories.",
